From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:14:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/common: Route every INTx pin of the CPU's PCIe root
 ports

intel_acpi_gen_def_acpi_pirq() writes one _PRT entry per device of the
root bus, for the pin that device uses. That is enough for the PCH root
ports, which have a _PRT of their own, but not for the graphics root
ports of the CPU (PEG, device 1), which have none: the functions behind
them interrupt through the root bus with whatever pin they use, and only
INTA had an entry. On a ThinkPad W541 the HD audio function of the
NVIDIA GPU (01:00.1, INTB, without MSI in snd_hda_intel) was left
without an interrupt: "can't derive routing for PCI INT B", "unable to
grab IRQ", so no audio on the outputs of the dGPU.

For a bridge of the CPU, write entries for all four pins. Devices of the
CPU route their pins 1:1 to PIRQA-D, as map_pirq() already assumes for
the pin of the port, and as the PEG _PRT of Intel's reference code does
(INTA-INTD to GSI 16-19).

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/common/rcba_pirq.c | 55 +++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/common/rcba_pirq.c b/src/southbridge/intel/common/rcba_pirq.c
index ae2214336..b0b3ce93f 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/common/rcba_pirq.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/common/rcba_pirq.c
@@ -44,6 +44,18 @@ static enum pirq map_pirq(const struct device *dev, const enum pci_pin pci_pin)
 	return (enum pirq)(pirq + PIRQ_A);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A PCI-to-PCI bridge of the CPU on the root bus, a PCIe root port for
+ * graphics (PEG): unlike the root ports of the PCH, it has no _PRT of its
+ * own, so the functions behind it interrupt through the routing of the root
+ * bus, with whatever pin they use.
+ */
+static bool is_cpu_bridge(const struct device *dev)
+{
+	return PCI_SLOT(dev->path.pci.devfn) < MIN_SLOT &&
+	       (dev->hdr_type & 0x7f) == PCI_HEADER_TYPE_BRIDGE;
+}
+
 void intel_acpi_gen_def_acpi_pirq(const struct device *lpc)
 {
 	struct slot_pin_irq_map *pin_irq_map;
@@ -72,22 +84,33 @@ void intel_acpi_gen_def_acpi_pirq(const struct device *lpc)
 		if (int_pin < PCI_INT_A || int_pin > PCI_INT_D)
 			continue;
 
-		if (is_slot_pin_assigned(pin_irq_map, map_count, pci_dev, int_pin))
-			continue;
-
-		enum pirq pirq = map_pirq(dev, int_pin);
-		if (pirq == PIRQ_INVALID)
-			continue;
-
-		pin_irq_map[map_count].slot = pci_dev;
-		pin_irq_map[map_count].pin = (enum pci_pin)int_pin;
-		pin_irq_map[map_count].pic_pirq = pirq;
-		/* PIRQs are mapped to GSIs starting at 16 */
-		pin_irq_map[map_count].apic_gsi = 16 + pirq_idx(pirq);
-		printk(BIOS_SPEW, "ACPI_PIRQ_GEN: %s: pin=%d pirq=%zd\n",
-		       dev_path(dev), int_pin - PCI_INT_A,
-		       pirq_idx(pin_irq_map[map_count].pic_pirq));
-		map_count++;
+		/*
+		 * The pin of the device, or all four for a CPU bridge: the HD
+		 * audio function of a graphics card behind it uses INTB.
+		 */
+		const bool all_pins = is_cpu_bridge(dev);
+		const unsigned int first = all_pins ? PCI_INT_A : int_pin;
+		const unsigned int last = all_pins ? PCI_INT_D : int_pin;
+
+		for (unsigned int pin = first; pin <= last; pin++) {
+			if (is_slot_pin_assigned(pin_irq_map, map_count, pci_dev,
+						 (enum pci_pin)pin))
+				continue;
+
+			enum pirq pirq = map_pirq(dev, (enum pci_pin)pin);
+			if (pirq == PIRQ_INVALID)
+				continue;
+
+			pin_irq_map[map_count].slot = pci_dev;
+			pin_irq_map[map_count].pin = (enum pci_pin)pin;
+			pin_irq_map[map_count].pic_pirq = pirq;
+			/* PIRQs are mapped to GSIs starting at 16 */
+			pin_irq_map[map_count].apic_gsi = 16 + pirq_idx(pirq);
+			printk(BIOS_SPEW, "ACPI_PIRQ_GEN: %s: pin=%d pirq=%zd\n",
+			       dev_path(dev), pin - PCI_INT_A,
+			       pirq_idx(pin_irq_map[map_count].pic_pirq));
+			map_count++;
+		}
 	}
 
 	intel_write_pci_PRT("\\_SB.PCI0", pin_irq_map, map_count, &pirq_map);
